\def\@LN@column{1}
\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {2}{\ignorespaces Residual controller architecture. The measured/estimated observation $\bm  {o}_t$ feeds the base neural MPC ($\bm  {u}_{NN}=\pi _{NN}(\bm  {o}_t)$) and the residual SAC policy ($\bm  {a}_t=[a_f,a_r,a_h]$). The torque channels give $\Delta \bm  {u}=\text  {res\_scale}\cdot [a_f,a_r]$, the horizon channel selects $N=\mathrm  {map}(a_h)$, and the applied torque is $\bm  {u}_t=\mathrm  {clip}(\bm  {u}_{NN}+\Delta \bm  {u},-\tau _{\max },\tau _{\max })$. Sensor faults and uncertainty enter the plant loop. The base network has 13 inputs; the adaptive residual observation has 15 components.}}{17}{figure.2}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:arch}{{2}{17}{Residual controller architecture. The measured/estimated observation $\bm o_t$ feeds the base neural MPC ($\bm u_{NN}=\pi _{NN}(\bm o_t)$) and the residual SAC policy ($\bm a_t=[a_f,a_r,a_h]$). The torque channels give $\Delta \bm u=\text {res\_scale}\cdot [a_f,a_r]$, the horizon channel selects $N=\mathrm {map}(a_h)$, and the applied torque is $\bm u_t=\mathrm {clip}(\bm u_{NN}+\Delta \bm u,-\tmax ,\tmax )$. Sensor faults and uncertainty enter the plant loop. The base network has 13 inputs; the adaptive residual observation has 15 components}{figure.2}{}}
